{"id": "EUVD-2026-102261", "enisaUuid": "38a90ebe-b49f-323f-ac83-bdb715c0e062", "description": "libfwsi through 20260522 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in libfwsi_mtp_file_entry_values_read_data() that allows attackers to read past buffer bounds via crafted MTP file entry shell items. Attackers can embed a 10 to 73 byte shell item with item data size of 44 or more in .lnk files, jump lists or shell bags to crash libfwsi consumers.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:57:28", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libfwsi-mtp-values-oob-read", "https://github.com/libyal/libfwsi/blob/2f2aba25b888f37314a39d8c3e71c0e3ced56e59/libfwsi/libfwsi_mtp_file_entry_values.c#L245-L267", "https://github.com/libyal/libfwsi", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libfwsi-through-20260522-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-libfwsi-mtp-file-entry-values-read-data"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111134", "GHSA-6mh6-95hc-pr4c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c49a3bb1-adaa-30bd-9529-5b0eb9dc1a70", "product": {"name": "libfwsi", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226420260522"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1d0786d4-b52b-3f85-9529-ac75c823d680", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}], "isExploited": false}